    {
      "id": "el992146916",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 622,
      "y": 490,
      "width": 473.3,
      "height": 131.2,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 999679163,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1757224717,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "WHY AN 80 GB CARD\nTwo workers x 38,000 MiB = 76,000 MiB.\n\nOn a 40 GB card a slice would be 19,500 MiB:\nafter 15.3 GiB of weights only ~2-4 GiB is left\nfor KV = ~17,000-27,000 tokens, 2-3 full-length\nsequences.  (on paper only, never run)",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "WHY AN 80 GB CARD\nTwo workers x 38,000 MiB = 76,000 MiB.\n\nOn a 40 GB card a slice would be 19,500 MiB:\nafter 15.3 GiB of weights only ~2-4 GiB is left\nfor KV = ~17,000-27,000 tokens, 2-3 full-length\nsequences.  (on paper only, never run)",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
